From e8b73e22adb30638ed816758965502cd5bee0a6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Akers <mike.akers@onepeloton.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 20:42:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 079/110] fix: clarify --max-concurrent flag as spawn-rate
 throttle, not concurrency limit (gt-dop) (#3659)

The flag description said "Limit concurrent polecat spawns" which implies
it caps simultaneously running polecats. In reality it's a spawn-rate
throttle: spawns N, pauses ~6s, resets counter, spawns N more. All
polecats remain running concurrently.

Updated flag description, help text, code comments, and runtime messages
across sling.go, sling_batch.go, scheduler_convoy.go, and
scheduler_epic.go to accurately describe the batch-throttle behavior.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 internal/cmd/scheduler_convoy.go | 2 +-
 internal/cmd/scheduler_epic.go   | 2 +-
 internal/cmd/sling.go            | 6 +++---
 internal/cmd/sling_batch.go      | 8 +++++---
 4 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/internal/cmd/scheduler_convoy.go b/internal/cmd/scheduler_convoy.go
index 98ba658c..42ed5b4f 100644
